WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.940
How does one small change at a synapse become a correction that arrives on time?

2
00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:13.233
David Marr and James Albus proposed that the climbing fibre is a teacher.

3
00:00:14.093 --> 00:00:15.673
But which way would it change a synapse?

4
00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:17.893
Marr guessed stronger.

5
00:00:17.893 --> 00:00:19.673
Albus guessed weaker.

6
00:00:20.683 --> 00:00:25.383
In 1982, Masao Ito and Masanobu Kano tested it in rabbits.

7
00:00:26.583 --> 00:00:27.583
Compare three conditions.

8
00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:29.877
Parallel fibres alone.

9
00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:31.797
No lasting depression.

10
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.190
Climbing fibre alone.

11
00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.450
No lasting depression either.

12
00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:43.093
The two together. Afterwards the parallel-fibre response is smaller, and it stays

13
00:00:43.093 --> 00:00:44.373
smaller for at least an hour.

14
00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:48.597
Under these conditions, only pairing weakened the synapse.

15
00:00:49.377 --> 00:00:53.077
This is cerebellar long-term depression, the sign Albus had chosen.

16
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.010
The input to a brake gets weaker.

17
00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.650
Does the nucleus fire more, or less?

18
00:01:04.683 --> 00:01:06.523
More, with other inputs unchanged.

19
00:01:07.503 --> 00:01:11.403
The foot presses the brake less, so the nucleus, already running, speeds up.

20
00:01:12.263 --> 00:01:13.603
Two negatives make a positive.

21
00:01:14.683 --> 00:01:16.563
But which parallel fibres are weakened?

22
00:01:17.463 --> 00:01:18.563
It depends on the region.

23
00:01:19.423 --> 00:01:23.983
In the flocculus, it is those active about a hundred and twenty milliseconds before

24
00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:24.983
the climbing fibre.

25
00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:30.917
That matters, because a visual error reaches the flocculus roughly a tenth of a

26
00:01:30.917 --> 00:01:32.017
second after the mistake.

27
00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:37.987
So the fibres active just before carry the context in which the mistake was made.

28
00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:43.690
Next time that context arrives, the learned change can act before the late visual

29
00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:46.850
error does. The correction need not wait for feedback.

30
00:01:47.983 --> 00:01:50.083
What does learning look like in a real cell?

31
00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:54.543
Monkeys returned a handle to a set position, and then the load changed.

32
00:01:55.533 --> 00:02:00.833
Climbing-fibre events show as big complex spikes; ordinary output spikes are simple

33
00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:06.273
spikes. In some recorded cells, complex spikes grew more frequent as the monkeys

34
00:02:06.273 --> 00:02:10.193
adapted. Simple-spike responses fell, and stayed lower.

35
00:02:11.217 --> 00:02:15.017
That pattern fits the rule, though it does not measure the synapse directly.

36
00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.880
But depression alone can only release the brake.

37
00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.560
What if the output needs to fall instead?

38
00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:31.470
One way: strengthen the same synapses, so the brake presses harder.

39
00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:36.230
Parallel-fibre activity without a paired climbing fibre can do that.

40
00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.490
Other circuit changes can also lower output.

41
00:02:40.483 --> 00:02:45.583
In this one simplified channel, weakening alone can only raise the output, with

42
00:02:45.583 --> 00:02:46.703
other inputs fixed.

43
00:02:47.663 --> 00:02:49.243
Strengthening can reverse that change.

44
00:02:50.233 --> 00:02:51.493
The rule has limits.

45
00:02:52.373 --> 00:02:54.633
The teacher works in some tasks and not others.

46
00:02:55.633 --> 00:02:59.053
Mice without detectable depression still learned the tested tasks.

47
00:03:00.053 --> 00:03:01.913
Climbing fibres also signal reward.

48
00:03:02.917 --> 00:03:07.777
The takeaway: in this model, a well-timed error signal can weaken the eligible

49
00:03:07.777 --> 00:03:13.357
synapses. With other inputs fixed, less brake means more output, ready before the

50
00:03:13.357 --> 00:03:14.617
late feedback next time.
